rvice.ServiceLoaderFeature`: it calls `computeIfAbsent` on an immutable `Map.of()`, causing `UnsupportedOperationException` before native tests run. Consequently, no dynamic-access input was produced and coverage is unavailable. Metrics record failure with 0 generated LOC, 0 metadata entries, and identical starting/ending commits. The preserved branch contains only a partial `TypedSubscriberTest`; the scaffold placeholder and empty metadata remain.\n\nInspect:\n- `human-intervention-logs/io.micronaut:micronaut-core-reactive:5.1.3/gradle-test/gradle-test-2026-10-02T09-44-06-040513Z.log`\n- `human-intervention-logs/io.micronaut:micronaut-core-reactive:5.1.3/dynamic-access-report/generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport-2026-10-02T09-18-02-087514Z.log`\n- `human-intervention-logs/io.micronaut:micronaut-core-reactive:5.1.3/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-10-02T09-24-15-953099Z.log`\n\nManual next steps:\n1. Reproduce `nativeTestCompile` from the preserved branch across the required GraalVM lanes and confirm the Micronaut/GraalVM compatibility boundary.\n2. Check for an upstream Micronaut fix or a consumer-realistic dependency/resource setup that avoids the empty immutable service map without patching the library or adding an unjustified Native Image flag.\n3. If a compliant resolution exists, complete the meaningful test suite and rerun metadata generation, dynamic-access reporting, and coordinate tests; otherwise report/link the upstream defect and mark this version unsupported.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_020c6a3449520286016abf7da4761487d19acbadc35060d183\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 13896, "output": 1369, "cacheRead": 178048, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 874, "totalTokens": 193313, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "stop", "timestamp": 1790934418284, "responseId": "resp_020c6a344